# ---------------------------------------------------------------- congregation, teen (cycle s2)

== what the congregation expects of the young
tier: life event
clash: congregation
band: teen
stages: juvenile young_adult
age: 11-19
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: faith, family
horizon: months
roles: parent, grandparent, friend, elder
earth: the congregation expects something of {N} this year, the family expects it too, and {N} is not sure it is right
tribal: the elders expect something of {N} at the next rite, the family expects it too, and {N} is not sure
magic: the temple expects something of {N} at the turning of the year, and {N} is not sure it is right
scene: At the door after the gathering, {clash.holder} spoke to {Ns} family: {clash.demand}. The family expects it too. {N} is not sure it is right for {N}, and going along with it would mean something.
scene tribal: At the fire, the elders have said what is expected of {N} at the next rite: {clash.demand}. The family's place in the clan rests on it. {N} is not sure it is {Ns} own.
scene magic: At the turning of the year the novices are named, and the word from {clash.holder} is plain: {clash.demand}. {Ns} name is already in the book. {N} is not sure it is right.
- W | do what is asked, at every gathering, as the family always has | v: tradition, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 90
- U | ask {parent} for a year's wait, to decide when older | v: self-direction, security | clash: leave | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 55
- B | find the young people's group that debates the big questions, and soon lead it | v: power, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place faith.seeking | chance: 70
- R | tell {clash.ally} how you feel, all of it, and ask for help | v: stimulation, benevolence | clash: bridge | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
- G | tell {clash.holder} the old ways deserve someone who means them | v: tradition, universalism | clash: confront | foot: lesson doubt can be said kindly | chance: 50
- W>B | join the volunteers who visit the care home, and serve that way | v: conformity, achievement | clash: own_scene | foot: place care.houses | chance: 75
- U>R | ask {clash.holder} the questions you really have, and see if there is room | v: self-direction, stimulation | clash: bridge | foot: person mentor | chance: 50
- B>G | say you will do it only if you may do it your own way | v: power, tradition | clash: confront | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 40
- R>W | go to the classes the congregation runs, and learn what is asked | v: security, conformity | clash: give_in | foot: place faith.congregation | chance: 90
- G>U | spend the summer at {grandparent}'s, away from it all, to think it through | v: tradition, self-direction | clash: leave | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 60
works: The matter is put off a year, with the family's grudging blessing, and {N} has time to find out what {N} thinks.
works: {N} finds a way to do what is asked partly in {Ns} own way, and nobody objects.
fails: Nothing changes. {N} goes along with it, and the doubt is still there afterwards.
fails: It half works: {clash.holder} agrees to wait, and the family talks of little else all summer.

